it became clear very soon after arriving  yesterday they weren't going to find any  more uh survivors uh in this burnt out  wreckage uh that i'll give you a look at  behind me and certainly that has been  confirmed now by uh authorities that  they are no longer looking for survivors  this is a recovery operation uh 18  people have been confirmed  to have died so far in in this attack  but there are still many many missing  some have been found in hospital there  were 40 people reported missing uh  initially some of those have been found  in hospital but certainly more than half  uh remain missing so uh it is feared  that the  death toll will grow human remains have  been uh recovered uh from the site and  relatives who are looking for their  loved ones that are giving their dna to  a local police station in the hope of uh  getting some news and some answers as to  what happened uh but away from this uh  very grim recovery operation now is also  a war crimes investigation there were  investigator investigators down here  yesterday a large number of them  and certainly as evidence has emerged to  show that there was a missile strike  on this shopping center something russia  denies and in his overnight  address president zielenski actually  released cctv footage himself very  dramatic images to show a missile uh  hitting this shopping center in  kremenchuk this industrial town in the  heart of ukraine uh so certainly uh  prosecutors and investigators will be  pouring over this evidence now uh to try  and uh work out whether this was a  deliberate hit something that president  zielinski says  it was but  aside from whether they managed to prove  if russia intentionally targeted this  shopping center what it doesn't change  is the fact that attacks on civilian  areas like this continue  to happen and ukrainian people continue  to feel  at risk country-wide here these missile  strikes  are across the country not just in the  eastern donbass region or on the capital  kiev